8. Decisions Deferred on Purpose (and why)
Taken from the architecture review — these are real needs, just not MVP-blocking ones:

Full workout_card_versions table. The snapshot-on-assignment pattern in §3.9 already solves the "old client's history shouldn't silently change" problem. Revisit if Discover needs to show a public template's changelog, or trainers need to explicitly branch a card into "v2."
Full workout_sessions → exercise_logs → set_logs model. Correct long-term shape for rich analytics (rest-timer, per-set RPE trends), but more schema than the current flat workout_logs needs to carry before there's usage data to justify it.
Video CDN: Mux vs Cloudflare Stream vs raw Supabase Storage for public Discover at scale — unresolved.
organization_members role permissions matrix — owner/admin/trainer/client are named but their exact write boundaries (can an admin remove a trainer? reassign clients?) need to be spelled out before building gym-admin UI.
Wearable credential storage mechanism — credential_reference is modeled, but Supabase Vault vs an external secrets manager (e.g., Doppler, AWS Secrets Manager) is still an open choice.
Rate limiting on public card creation / follow spam — not yet addressed at the DB level.
