10.3 Connection flow — redeem-invite (Edge Function)
Look up the invite by code; check status, expires_at, uses_count < max_uses
Look up the subscription; check seats_used < seat_limit — if full, reject with "seats full" and notify the coach/org owner to upgrade
Create the coaching_relationships row (type = gym if owner_type = organization, else private), setting org_id if applicable
Increment invites.uses_count and subscriptions.seats_used
This is also how "Coach A has 20 real clients — how do those 20 people find the right coach" gets solved without search: the coach hands out their code/QR (in person, in a welcome email, printed at the gym desk); redemption is deterministic, not discovery-based.

10.4 Pricing ladder — open decision
Your example (₹1000/50 seats, ₹2000/100) is linear (₹20/seat flat). The alternative is degressive pricing, more standard for SaaS seat tiers, which rewards committing to a bigger tier upfront:

Tier	Seats	Linear (₹20/seat)	Degressive example
Starter	50	₹1,000	₹1,000 (₹20/seat)
Growth	100	₹2,000	₹1,800 (₹18/seat)
Pro	250	₹5,000	₹3,750 (₹15/seat)
Either is implementable identically in subscriptions.plan_tier/price_inr — this is a pricing decision, not a schema one.

